{"r":"xbw","lane":{"p":701,"e":[{"h":"خَبَتِ النَّارُ","t":["aor. ",[2,"تَخْبُو"],", inf. n. ",[2,"خُبُوٌّ"]," (JK, S, Msb, K) and ",[2,"خَبْوٌ"],", (K,) ",[1,"The fire became allayed; subsided;"]," (K;) ",[1,"became extinguished;"]," (S, K;) ",[1,"the flaming,"]," or ",[1,"blazing, of the fire ceased,"]," or ",[1,"became allayed"]," or ",[1,"extinguished."]," (JK, Msb.) [The verb is used, in this sense, of Hell, in the Kur xvii. 99.] ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"خَبَتِ الحَرْبُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The war became allayed, assuaged,"]," or ",[1,"appeased;"]," (JK, K, TA;) ",[1,"became extinguished."]," (K, TA.) And ",[2,"خَبَتْ حِدَّةُ النَّاقَةِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The sharpness,"]," or ",[1,"irascibility, of the she-camel became allayed, assuaged,"]," or ",[1,"appeased."]," (JK, K, * TA.) And ",[2,"خَبَا لَهَبُهُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The heat,"]," or ",[1,"vehemence, of his anger became allayed, assuaged,"]," or ",[1,"appeased."]," (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"اخبى النَّارَ","t":[[1,"He extinguished the fire;"]," (S, K;) ",[1,"he allayed,"]," or ",[1,"extinguished, the flaming,"]," or ",[1,"blazing, of the fire."]," (JK, Msb.) ― -b2- And [hence,] ",[2,"اخبى الحَرْبَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He extinguished"]," [or ",[1,"allayed"],"] ",[1,"the fire of the war."]," (K, TA.) And ",[2,"اخبى حِدَّةَ النَّاقَهِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He extinguished"]," [or ",[1,"allayed"],"] ",[1,"the sharpness,"]," or ",[1,"irascibility, of the she-camel."]," (K, * TA.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"خِبَآءٌ","t":["accord. to some belongs to this art. (TA in art. ",[2,"خبأ"],".) See arts. ",[2,"خبأ"]," and ",[2,"خبى"],"."]}]},"mufradat":["خبت النار تخبو: سكن لهبها، وصار عليها خباء من رماد، أي غشاء، وأصل الخباء الغطاء الذي يتغطى به، وقيل لغشاء السنبلة خباء، قال عز وجل: كلما خبت زدناهم سعيرا [الإسراء/ 97] ."]}